 R←Test_SendEmail_05(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕IO;⎕ML;⎕TRAP;parms;rc;msg;log;text;filename1;filename2;parts;lines
⍝ Send an email with two attachments: a PDF file and an HTML file; check the closing boundary
 ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 parms←∆NewMail'Subject from APL Team SMTP: ',⊃⎕SI
 parms.Body←'Simple text'
 filename1←'./Test-Files/APL-Code.pdf'
 parms.AddAttachment filename1'application/pdf'
 filename2←'./Test-Files/CrashReport.html'
 parms.AddAttachment filename2'text/html'
 (rc msg log text)←∆Send parms
 →T.PassesIf 0=rc
 parts←∆MimeParts ∆Unstuff text                  ⍝ Fails without a closing boundary
 →T.PassesIf 3=≢parts
 →T.PassesIf(∆ReadBytes filename1)≡∆PartBytes 2⊃parts
 →T.PassesIf(∆ReadBytes filename2)≡∆PartBytes 3⊃parts
 lines←SMTP.Message.SplitLines text
 lines←lines/⍨0<≢¨lines
 →T.PassesIf'--'≡¯2↑⊃⌽lines                       ⍝ The closing boundary is the last line

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
